===Format===
* '''Group Stage:''' June 22''<sup>nd</sup>'' - July 14''<sup>th</sup>'', 2024
** Two Single Round-Robin groups (Cross-group play was in '''[[VCT/2024/Americas_League/Stage_1|Stage 1]]''')
*** Group Alpha has 5 teams & Group Omega has 6 teams, both drawn before Stage 1 based on '''[[VCT/2024/Americas_League/Kickoff|Kickoff]]''' performance
**** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for how the groups were drawn''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="margin-left:45px">
* 1 team from '''Pot 1''' – {{Bgcolortext|seedup|Top 2 teams}} that also competed at '''[[VCT/2024/Stage 1/Masters|Masters Madrid]]''' ([[Sentinels]] and [[LOUD]])
** Furthermore, Sentinels were placed into Group Alpha as the Kickoff winner, while LOUD was placed into Group Omega as the Kickoff runner-up
* 1 team from '''Pot 2''' – Playoff {{Bgcolortext|up|semifinalists}} ([[Evil Geniuses]] and [[NRG]])
* 1 team from '''Pot 3''' – Teams that {{Bgcolortext|up|advanced to the Play-In}} ([[G2 Esports]] and [[MIBR]])
* 1 team from '''Pot 4''' – Teams that were {{Bgcolortext|down|eliminated in the group stage but did not finish last in their groups}} ([[Cloud9]] and [[Leviatán]])
* 1-2 teams from '''Pot 5''' – Teams that were {{Bgcolortext|down|eliminated in the group stage after finishing last in their groups}} ([[FURIA Esports]], [[100 Thieves]] and [[KRÜ Esports]])
</div></div>
* All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** Starting from '''Regular Season''', [[Haven]] replaces [[Breeze]] in the map pool.
** {{Bgcolortext|up|Top 6 teams}} with the best combined records from '''[[VCT/2024/Americas League/Stage 1|Stage 1]]''' and '''[[VCT/2024/Americas League/Stage_2#Group Stage|Stage 2]]''', regardless of groups, will advance to '''Playoffs'''
*** {{Bgcolortext|seedup|Top 2 teams}} earn a bye to the '''Upper Bracket Semifinals'''
*** {{Bgcolortext|up|3<sup>rd</sup> through 6<sup>th</sup> place teams}} advance to the '''Knockout Round'''
** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="margin-left:45px">
*2-way tie
*# Head-to-head Match Score
*3-way tie
*# Head-to-head Match Series
*#*Team with a two matchup head-to-head advantage automatically receives first of the group. Tie-breakers for the remaining two teams are determined using the above head-to-head tiebreaker process.
*#*If no team has a two matchup head-to-head advantage (all Teams are 1-1 head-to-head), then proceed to next step of the 3-way tie-breaker process.
*# Map differential
*# Round differential
*# Tiebreaker {{Abbr/Bo1}} match
*4+-way tie
*# Map differential
*# Round differential
*# Map differential among the tied teams
*# Round differential among the tied teams
*#* If the ties are reduced to less than 3 teams after this process, tiebreakers for the respective number of teams must be used to break ties among them.
</div></div>

* '''Playoffs:''' July 17''<sup>th</sup>'' - July 21''<sup>st</sup>'', 2024
** Hybrid-Elimination bracket
** '''Knockout Round''' is '''Single-Elimination'''
** '''Upper Bracket Semifinals''' onwards is '''Double-Elimination'''
** All matches ''(excl. Lower Bracket Final & Grand Final)'' are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** Lower Bracket Final & Grand Final are {{Abbr/Bo5}}
*** Starting from '''Playoffs''', [[Abyss]] replaces [[Split]] in the map pool.
** {{Bgcolortext|up|Top 3 teams}} will qualify for '''[[VCT/2024/Champions|Champions]]'''

