===Format===
* '''Group Stage''': April ''6<sup>th</sup>'' - April ''29<sup>th</sup>, 2024''
** Two Single Round-Robin groups
*** Group Alpha has 5 teams & Group Omega has 6 teams, both drawn before Stage 1 based on '''[[VCT/2024/Pacific_League/Kickoff|Kickoff]]''' performance
**** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for how the groups were drawn''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="margin-left:45px">
* 1 team from '''Pot 1''' – {{Bgcolortext|seedup|Top 2 teams}} that also competed at '''[[VCT/2024/Stage 1/Masters|Masters Madrid]]''' ([[Gen.G Esports]] and [[Paper Rex]])
** Furthermore, Gen.G was placed into Group Alpha as the Kickoff winner, while Paper Rex was placed into Group Omega as the Kickoff runner-up
* 1 team from '''Pot 2''' – Playoff {{Bgcolortext|up|semifinalists}} ([[T1]] and [[DRX]])
* 1 team from '''Pot 3''' – Teams that {{Bgcolortext|up|advanced to the Play-In}} ([[Team Secret]] and [[ZETA DIVISION]])
* 1 team from '''Pot 4''' – Teams that were {{Bgcolortext|down|eliminated in the group stage but did not finish last in their groups}} ([[Global Esports]] and [[Talon Esports]])
* 1-2 teams from '''Pot 5''' – Teams that were {{Bgcolortext|down|eliminated in the group stage after finishing last in their groups}} ([[Bleed Esports]], [[DetonatioN FocusMe]] and [[Rex Regum Qeon]])
</div></div>
*** Teams will play cross-group matches
*** All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
*** {{Bgcolortext|up|Top 3 teams}} from each group advance to '''Playoffs'''
**** {{Bgcolortext|seedup|Winners}} have a bye into the '''Upper Bracket Semifinals'''
**** {{Bgcolortext|up|2<sup>nd</sup> & 3<sup>rd</sup> place teams}} advance to the '''Knockout Round'''''
*** Each team also needs at least '''two wins''' to qualify for the playoffs. If this rule is not met, the highest-ranked team from the other group that meets this criteria and has not already advanced qualifies instead.
** <span class="mw-customtoggle-Tiebreaker" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-Tiebreaker" style="margin-left:45px">
*2-way tie
*# Head-to-head Match Score
*3-way tie
*# Head-to-head Match Series
*#*Teams with two matchup head-to-head advantage automatically receives first of the group. Tie-breakers for the remaining two teams are determined using the above head-to-head tiebreaker process.
*#*If no team has a two matchup head-to-head advantage (all Teams are 1-1 head-to-head), then proceed to next step of the 3-way tie-breaker process.
*# Map differential
*# Round differential
*# Tiebreaker {{Abbr/Bo1}} match
*4+-way tie
*# Map differential
*# Round differential
*# Map differential among the tied teams
*# Round differential among the tied teams
*#* If ties reduced to less than 3 teams after this process, tiebreakers for respective number of teams must be used to break ties among them.
</div></div>

* '''Playoffs''': May ''3<sup>rd</sup>'' - May ''12<sup>th</sup>, 2024''
** Hybrid-Elimination bracket
** '''Knockout Round''' is '''Single-Elimination'''
** '''Upper Bracket Semifinals''' onwards is '''Double-Elimination'''
** All matches ''(excl. Lower Bracket Final & Grand Final)'' are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** Lower Bracket Final & Grand Final are {{Abbr/Bo5}}
** {{Bgcolortext|up|Top 3 teams}} will qualify for '''[[VCT/2024/Stage 2/Masters|Masters Shanghai]]'''

