===Format===
*'''Swiss Stage:''' ''May 23<sup>rd</sup> – 27<sup>th</sup>, 2024''
** 8 team Swiss System format
*** All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
*** In Round 1, each 2nd-seeded team is matched against a 3rd-seeded team from a different region
**** Draw for Round 1 was done by [[Victoria Horsley|Victoria]] & [[Ender]] live at the Los Angeles Riot Games Arena after the Americas Stage 1 Grand Final
*** Rounds 2 and 3 are seeded based on each team's win-loss record
**** Intra-regional matchups are now permitted
**** In Round 2, the first team drawn for each matchup is the higher seed for map selection purposes
**** Teams cannot be drawn against each other multiple times in this phase. If this happens, then the second of those teams is moved to the next valid slot.
**** When determining order of play, teams are not scheduled for back-to-back matches in this stage
**** Draws for Rounds 2 and 3 were done by [[Victoria Horsley|Victoria]] & [[Yinsu]] live at the Valo Arena 
***** Round 2 draw was done after the conclusion of Round 1
***** Round 3 draw was done after the conclusion of Round 2
** {{Bgcolortext|up|Teams that reach 2 wins}} advance to '''Playoffs'''
** {{Bgcolortext|down|Teams that reach 2 losses}} are eliminated

*'''Playoffs:''' ''May 30<sup>th</sup> – June 9<sup>th</sup>, 2024''
** 8 teams: 4 Top-seeded teams & 4 Swiss Stage teams 
** Double-Elimination bracket
** Top-seeded teams pick their upper bracket quarterfinal opponents from the Swiss Stage teams in random order
*** Order drawn: [[Paper Rex]]. then [[100 Thieves]], then [[EDward Gaming]], leaving [[Fnatic]] with last remaining Swiss Stage qualifier
*** Picks were done live at the Valo Arena with [[Victoria Horsley|Victoria]], [[Yinsu]], [[唯嘉|Valora]] and representatives from each top seed after the conclusion of the Swiss Stage
** All matches ''(excl. Lower Final and Grand Final)'' are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
** Lower Final and Grand Final are {{Abbr/Bo5}}

